  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste Police Development Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is phase four of the Timor-Leste Police Development Program delivered by the Australian Federal Police. The overarching objective of the program is for the Timorese police to deliver skilled and professional policing services, which respond effectively to community needs and contribute to a stable and secure Timor-Leste. There are three core components of the program that set out to achieve this goal: 1) Sustainability, self-improvement and organisational leadership; 2) Operational effectiveness; and 3) Responsive policing services. Phase five began on 1 January 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
